<title>GERMANY: Waigel sees no threat to deficit goals.</title>
<headline>Waigel sees no threat to deficit goals.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Friday he sees no threat to his projection that the 1997 budget deficit would be 3.0 percent of gross domestic product.</p>
<p>Waigel told journalists the deficit would fall clearly below that level in 1998.</p>
<p>Waigel said the government would be in a position to profit again from shares in Deutsche Telekom it sold to the Kreditanstalt fuer Wiederaufbau (KFW) when the KFW resold those shares to the market.</p>
</text>
